.\" Man page for OneCloudRiver
.\" Generated for version 0.1.4
.TH ONECLOUDRIVER 1 "2026-08-04" "OneCloudRiver 0.1.4" "User Manual"
.SH NAME
onecloudriver \- Native OneDrive filesystem for Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B onecloudriver
\fI\,command\/\fR [\fI\,options\/\fR]
.br
.B onecloudriver mount
\fI\,mount_point\/\fR \fB\-a\fR \fI\,account\/\fR [\fI\,flags\/\fR]
.br
.B onecloudriver account
\fI\,subcommand\/\fR [\fI\,options\/\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
OneCloudRiver mounts your OneDrive as a FUSE filesystem on Linux,
allowing you to read, write, create, and delete files directly from the
file manager and the terminal.
.P
It also provides CLI commands to operate on OneDrive without mounting
(list, upload, download, create folders, copy, move, rename, delete, sync).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B mount \fImount_point\fR
Mounts OneDrive in the specified directory as a FUSE filesystem.
Requires \fB\-a\fR \fIaccount\fR.
.TP
.B account add
Adds a new Microsoft account via OAuth2.
.TP
.B account list
Lists the configured accounts.
.TP
.B account remove \fIaccount\fR
Removes an account. Use \fB\-\-purge\fR to also delete the cache without
asking, or \fB\-\-keep\fR to keep it.
.TP
.B list \fI[path]\fR
Lists files in the root or in the specified path. Requires \fB\-a\fR \fIaccount\fR.
.TP
.B upload \fIfile\fR \fI[remote_path]\fR
Uploads a local file to OneDrive. Requires \fB\-a\fR \fIaccount\fR.
.TP
.B download \fIremote_path\fR
Downloads a file from OneDrive to the local disk. Requires \fB\-a\fR \fIaccount\fR.
.TP
.B mkdir \fIpath\fR
Creates a folder in OneDrive. Requires \fB\-a\fR \fIaccount\fR.
.TP
.B copy \fIsource\fR \fIdestination\fR
Copies a file or folder. Requires \fB\-a\fR \fIaccount\fR.
.TP
.B mv \fIsource\fR \fIdestination\fR
Moves a file or folder. Requires \fB\-a\fR \fIaccount\fR.
.TP
.B rename \fIpath\fR \fInew_name\fR
Renames a file or folder. Requires \fB\-a\fR \fIaccount\fR.
.TP
.B rm \fIpath\fR
Deletes a file or folder. Requires \fB\-a\fR \fIaccount\fR.
.TP
.B info \fIpath\fR
Shows detailed information (ID, size, dates). Requires \fB\-a\fR \fIaccount\fR.
.TP
.B sync
Forces an immediate delta synchronization: applies the remote changes to the
account's persisted cache now and prints how many were applied, without
waiting for the background poll interval of a mount. Requires \fB\-a\fR
\fIaccount\fR. Works without a mount; a running mount holds the cache lock, so
stop the mount or service first.
.TP
.B completion \fIshell\fR
Generates the completion script for the specified shell (bash, zsh, fish).
.TP
.B service \fIsubcommand\fR
Manages the systemd user service for auto-mount on login (install, uninstall,
status, start, stop). See the SERVICE COMMAND section below.
.SH SERVICE COMMAND
The
.B service
command manages a user systemd service that automatically mounts OneDrive on
login. It installs a template unit
(\fI~/.config/systemd/user/onecloudriver@.service\fR) so that each configured
account is mounted independently: one instance
(\fIonecloudriver@<account>.service\fR) per account.
.P
Subcommands:
.TP
.B service install [\fB\-\-mountpoint\fR \fIpath\fR] [\fB\-a\fR \fIaccount\fR] [\fB\-\-enable\fR] [\fB\-\-all\fR]
Creates the template unit, reloads systemd and, when
\fB\-\-enable\fR is given, enables and starts the instance. The mountpoint
directory is created automatically if it does not exist. If
\fB\-\-mountpoint\fR is omitted, a saved mountpoint is used only when it
contains the \fI%i\fR instance placeholder. A concrete path saved by the
interactive mount command is ignored with a warning to prevent account
collisions in the shared template. The fallback is \fI~/OneDrive/%i\fR
(\fI%i\fR is replaced by the account name).
.TP
.B service uninstall [\fB\-\-all\fR]
Stops and disables all instances and removes the template unit.
.TP
.B service list
Lists all installed instantiated onecloudriver user-service units, including
disabled, stopped and never-started instances. Shows the account, enabled state,
active state, sub-state and mountpoint.
.TP
.B service status [\fIaccount\fR]
With an account, shows a concise state summary including the PID and mountpoint.
For failed, stopped or restarting units, it also shows the last 10 journal lines.
Without an account, lists the active instances and the installed unit path.
A successfully queried failed unit returns exit code 0.
.TP
.B service start \fIaccount\fR
Starts the instance for the given account.
.TP
.B service stop [\fIaccount\fR] [\fB\-\-all\fR]
Stops the instance and unmounts its FUSE filesystem.
.P
Flags:
.TP
\fB\-\-mountpoint\fR \fIpath\fR
Base mount path for the instance. Use \fI%i\fR for the account placeholder.
.TP
\fB\-a\fR, \fB\-\-account\fR \fIaccount\fR
Account to install the service for. If omitted, uses the only configured account.
.TP
\fB\-\-enable\fR
Enable and start the service immediately after installing it.
.TP
\fB\-\-all\fR
Apply the operation to all configured accounts.
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fIformat\fR
Output format for every \fBservice\fR subcommand: \fItext\fR (default),
\fIjson\fR or \fIyaml\fR. In structured modes, stdout carries exactly one
serialized document and diagnostics go to stderr.
.SH GLOBAL FLAGS
.TP
\fB--log-level\fR \fIlevel\fR
Minimum level written to the JSON log file. Supported values are
\fItrace\fR, \fIdebug\fR, \fIinfo\fR, \fIwarn\fR and \fIerror\fR. Default: \fIinfo\fR.
.TP
\fB--log-json\fR
Emit structured JSON logs to stderr instead of the on-disk log file
(systemd / journal friendly).
.TP
\fB-v\fR, \fB--version\fR
Prints the version of the binary (e.g. \fI0.1.4\fR) and exits.
.SH MOUNT FLAGS
.TP
\fB\-a\fR, \fB\-\-account\fR \fIaccount\fR
Microsoft account to use (required).
.TP
\fB\-\-cache\-dir\fR \fIdirectory\fR
Root directory for the cache. Default: \fI~/.cache/onecloudriver/<account>\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-cache\-ttl\fR \fIduration\fR
Metadata TTL. E.g.: \fI60s\fR, \fI5m\fR. Default: \fI60s\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-cache\-max\-entries\fR \fIn\fR
Maximum number of folders with cached children. Default: \fI2000\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-cache\-max\-size\fR \fIsize\fR
Maximum content cache size. E.g.: \fI1GB\fR, \fI500MB\fR. Default: \fI0\fR (unlimited).
.TP
\fB--debug\fR
Start a local expvar + pprof debug server on \fI127.0.0.1:6060\fR (loopback)
and raise the log level to debug.
.TP
\fB--debug-addr\fR \fIaddress\fR
Address for the \fB--debug\fR server. Default: \fI127.0.0.1:6060\fR. Only bind
another interface (e.g. \fI0.0.0.0:6060\fR) on a trusted network.
.SH ACCOUNT REMOVE FLAGS
.TP
\fB\-\-purge\fR
Deletes the local cache without asking.
.TP
\fB\-\-keep\fR
Keeps the local cache without asking.
.P
\fB\-\-purge\fR and \fB\-\-keep\fR are mutually exclusive. If neither is
specified, you are asked interactively.
.SH EXAMPLES
.P
Mount OneDrive:
.RS
.B onecloudriver mount ~/OneDrive -a user@outlook.com
.RE
.P
Mount with a custom cache:
.RS
.B onecloudriver mount ~/OneDrive -a user@outlook.com \-\-cache\-ttl 5m \-\-cache\-max\-size 2GB
.RE
.P
Add an account:
.RS
.B onecloudriver account add
.RE
.P
Remove an account with cleanup:
.RS
.B onecloudriver account remove user@outlook.com \-\-purge
.RE
.P
List files without mounting:
.RS
.B onecloudriver list -a user@outlook.com
.RE
.P
Force an immediate sync without mounting:
.RS
.B onecloudriver sync -a user@outlook.com
.RE
.P
Install and enable the service:
.RS
.B onecloudriver service install -a user@outlook.com \-\-enable
.RE
.SH OFFLINE MODE
If there is no internet connection when mounting, OneCloudRiver starts in
offline mode (read-only access to previously cached files).
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGINT, SIGTERM, SIGHUP
Cleanly unmount the filesystem (Ctrl+C, kill, terminal close).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/onecloudriver/
Account configuration (JSON).
.TP
.I ~/.cache/onecloudriver/<account>/
Metadata cache (BoltDB) and content (files on disk).
.TP
.I ~/.config/systemd/user/onecloudriver@.service
User systemd template unit installed by \fBservice install\fR.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
FUSE 3 (package \fIfuse3\fR). The user must belong to the \fIfuse\fR group.
.SH OBSERVABILITY
.P
The on-disk log \fI~/.config/onecloudriver/onecloudriver.log\fR is rotated by
size (10 MB per file, keeping at most 5 gzipped backups for up to 30 days) and
filters to Info+ by default, so it does not grow unbounded.
.P
Start a mount with \fB--debug\fR to inspect its internal state over HTTP on the
loopback interface:
.RS
.B onecloudriver mount ~/OneDrive -a user@outlook.com --debug
.br
.B curl 127.0.0.1:6060/debug/vars
.br
.B curl 127.0.0.1:6060/debug/pprof/
.RE
.P
/debug/vars exposes \fIcache_hits\fR, \fIcache_misses\fR,
\fIcache_evictions\fR, \fIinode_count\fR,\n\fIcontent_cache_total_size\fR, \fIuploads_in_flight\fR,
\fIuploads_completed\fR, \fIuploads_failed\fR, \fIdelta_sync_count\fR and
\fIdelta_error_count\fR.
.SH TROUBLESHOOTING
.SS "Device or resource busy"
Close file managers and terminals inside the mountpoint.
.RS
.B fusermount3 -u /path/to/mountpoint
.RE
.SS "Transport endpoint is not connected"
The process terminated unexpectedly.
.RS
.B fusermount3 -uz /path/to/mountpoint
.RE
.SS "Token error"
Re-authenticate the account:
.RS
.B onecloudriver account remove user@outlook.com
.br
.B onecloudriver account add
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fusermount3 (1),
.BR mount.fuse3 (8)
.P
Repository: \fIhttps://github.com/frosado/onecloudriver\fR
